WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.416 --> 00:00:33.083
<b>In the previous verse, </b>
<b>Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:38.250
<b>how He manifests in this world </b>
<b>through His divine power.</b>

3
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.208
<b>This raises the question:</b>

4
00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:42.625
<b>When does He do this?</b>

5
00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:44.458
<b>Why does He do this?</b>

6
00:00:44.458 --> 00:00:47.791
<b>This verse provides the answer.</b>

7
00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:55.541
<b>You may have heard this verse before –</b>

8
00:00:55.541 --> 00:01:00.333
<b>it's one of the most renowned verses from </b>
<b>both the Bhagavad Gita and the Mahabharata.</b>

9
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:01.333
<b>Here,</b>

10
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:06.041
<b>Lord Krishna reveals when </b>
<b>He appears in this world.</b>

11
00:01:06.041 --> 00:01:09.000
<b>Addressing Arjuna, He says,</b>

12
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.000
<b>"O descendant of Bharata Arjuna,</b>

13
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.416
<b>whenever righteousness declines</b>

14
00:01:14.416 --> 00:01:17.125
<b>and unrighteousness prevails,</b>

15
00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:21.375
<b>I manifest Myself on Earth."</b>

16
00:01:21.375 --> 00:01:25.791
<b>Krishna had already clarified </b>
<b>that He doesn't take birth,</b>

17
00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:28.958
<b>but rather manifests in this world.</b>

18
00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:34.458
<b>That's why the word 'srijamyaham' </b>
<b>is used in this verse –</b>

19
00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:38.083
<b>composed of 'srijami' and ‘aham’.</b>

20
00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:41.166
<b>‘srijami’ meaning 'to manifest'</b>

21
00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:44.291
<b>and 'aham' meaning 'I'.</b>

22
00:01:44.291 --> 00:01:48.666
<b>Together, 'srijamyaham' means </b>
<b>'I manifest Myself.'</b>

23
00:01:48.666 --> 00:01:49.583
<b>But</b>

24
00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:52.208
<b>when does Krishna manifest?</b>

25
00:01:52.208 --> 00:01:59.375
<b>He appears in various forms when righteousness </b>
<b>declines and unrighteousness rises.</b>

26
00:01:59.375 --> 00:02:02.083
<b>And where does He appear?</b>

27
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:03.291
<b>On Earth,</b>

28
00:02:03.291 --> 00:02:06.875
<b>Wherever such unrighteousness arises,</b>

29
00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:09.041
<b>Lord Krishna manifests Himself there.</b>

30
00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:15.916
<b>The form, timing, and location of His appearance </b>
<b>may vary according to circumstances.</b>

31
00:02:15.916 --> 00:02:20.000
<b>It's not necessary that He appears only in India.</b>

32
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.958
<b>He can manifest anywhere, and when He does,</b>

33
00:02:23.958 --> 00:02:29.791
<b>He imparts this divine knowledge to His chosen </b>
<b>one according to their capacity.</b>

34
00:02:29.791 --> 00:02:30.833
<b>Remember,</b>

35
00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:33.208
<b>just as a good teacher knows everything</b>

36
00:02:33.208 --> 00:02:38.250
<b>but explains according to the student's level,</b>

37
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.958
<b>Krishna does the same.</b>

38
00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:43.041
<b>In this righteous war of Mahabharata,</b>

39
00:02:43.041 --> 00:02:50.250
<b>Arjuna was among the most evolved beings, both </b>
<b>in personal capability and cultural strength.</b>

40
00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.208
<b>For this reason,</b>

41
00:02:51.208 --> 00:02:53.333
<b>in accordance with his capability,</b>

42
00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:57.958
<b>Lord Krishna chose him to receive the highest </b>
<b>description of this spiritual knowledge of the Gita.</b>

43
00:02:57.958 --> 00:02:59.166
<b>This verse</b>

44
00:02:59.166 --> 00:03:01.958
<b>also uses 'dharma glanih' –</b>

45
00:03:01.958 --> 00:03:03.416
<b>what does this mean?</b>

46
00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:06.625
<b>It means the decline of righteousness.</b>

47
00:03:06.625 --> 00:03:10.875
<b>When people begin to see material </b>
<b>success as everything,</b>

48
00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:14.375
<b>when selfishness and </b>
<b>exploitation reach their peak,</b>

49
00:03:14.375 --> 00:03:20.166
<b>when human values like compassion, mercy, </b>
<b>and gratitude begin to disappear –</b>

50
00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.666
<b>this is the decline of righteousness.</b>

51
00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:24.708
<b>This is exactly what happened in Mahabharata –</b>

52
00:03:24.708 --> 00:03:26.791
<b>the exploitation of Draupadi,</b>

53
00:03:26.791 --> 00:03:28.916
<b>the injustice against the Pandavas,</b>

54
00:03:28.916 --> 00:03:32.500
<b>Duryodhana's selfishness and ego at its peak.</b>

55
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.541
<b>In such times, Lord Krishna manifested Himself.</b>

56
00:03:35.541 --> 00:03:39.208
<b>This state of declining </b>
<b>righteousness isn't just social –</b>

57
00:03:39.208 --> 00:03:42.125
<b>it can exist in our hearts too.</b>

58
00:03:42.125 --> 00:03:44.291
<b>When our mind begins to get polluted,</b>

59
00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:49.875
<b>becomes selfish, gets entangled in desires, </b>
<b>fills with unrighteousness –</b>

60
00:03:49.875 --> 00:03:53.250
<b>that's when we should take refuge in Krishna</b>

61
00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.583
<b>and establish Him in our hearts.</b>

62
00:03:56.583 --> 00:04:04.750
<b>Krishna will support us by manifesting in our </b>
<b>hearts through His knowledge and remembrance.</b>

63
00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.250
<b>This verse gives us a ray of hope –</b>

64
00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:13.666
<b>when darkness in life reaches its peak, </b>
<b>don't despair.</b>

65
00:04:13.666 --> 00:04:17.125
<b>Simply take refuge in Lord Krishna –</b>

66
00:04:17.125 --> 00:04:24.375
<b>He is both capable of dispelling all </b>
<b>darkness and desires your welfare.</b>

67
00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:32.125
<b>As I told Arjuna,</b>

68
00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:36.916
<b>whenever darkness and despair loom,</b>

69
00:04:36.916 --> 00:04:41.291
<b>Clouds of spiritual and moral decline </b>
<b>loom overhead.</b>

70
00:04:41.291 --> 00:04:44.541
<b>and unrighteousness begins to prevail,</b>

71
00:04:44.541 --> 00:04:49.041
<b>I manifest Myself.</b>

72
00:04:49.041 --> 00:04:50.375
<b>But</b>

73
00:04:50.375 --> 00:04:52.416
<b>understand this –</b>

74
00:04:52.416 --> 00:04:59.041
<b>I'm not just speaking of </b>
<b>this material world or Earth...</b>

75
00:04:59.041 --> 00:05:04.250
<b>I am eager to enter your life too,</b>

76
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:09.416
<b>ready to manifest in your heart.</b>

77
00:05:09.416 --> 00:05:15.125
<b>Whenever despondency or </b>
<b>negativity starts to overcome you,</b>

78
00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:17.833
<b>when your spirit begins to falter,</b>

79
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:23.458
<b>I am just one prayer away.</b>

80
00:05:23.458 --> 00:05:29.166
<b>See your heart as the battlefield of Kurukshetra.</b>

81
00:05:29.166 --> 00:05:35.541
<b>Just as I guided Arjuna in his difficult times,</b>

82
00:05:35.541 --> 00:05:36.583
<b>similarly,</b>

83
00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:43.000
<b>I am always present to guide you too.</b>

84
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:49.875
<b>When doubt clouds your mind </b>
<b>and you begin to lose your way,</b>

85
00:05:49.875 --> 00:05:55.083
<b>that is your signal to call upon me.</b>

86
00:05:55.083 --> 00:06:00.875
<b>Praying with sincerity, </b>
<b>contemplating my teachings,</b>

87
00:06:00.875 --> 00:06:06.833
<b>or studying sacred texts isn't just </b>
<b>a display of devotion;</b>

88
00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:07.750
<b>but rather,</b>

89
00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:18.291
<b>it's also an invitation for me to enter your life and </b>
<b>dispel all darkness with the light of knowledge.</b>

90
00:06:18.291 --> 00:06:23.041
<b>Maintaining positive thoughts</b>
<b>even in adverse circumstances</b>

91
00:06:23.041 --> 00:06:27.708
<b>is like being in communion with me.</b>

92
00:06:27.708 --> 00:06:31.833
<b>When you focus on positivity,</b>

93
00:06:31.833 --> 00:06:38.166
<b>practice gratitude, and remember </b>
<b>your spiritual nature,</b>

94
00:06:38.166 --> 00:06:42.458
<b>you demonstrate your faith in me.</b>

95
00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:48.666
<b>You declare that even though </b>
<b>despair surrounds you,</b>

96
00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:54.708
<b>but you still believe in that divine goodness</b>

97
00:06:54.708 --> 00:06:57.916
<b>that pervades the entire universe.</b>

98
00:06:57.916 --> 00:06:59.333
<b>Remember,</b>

99
00:06:59.333 --> 00:07:05.166
<b>just as the sun rises unfailingly each day,</b>

100
00:07:05.166 --> 00:07:12.875
<b>it is my promise that I will manifest in your life</b>

101
00:07:12.875 --> 00:07:17.791
<b>whenever you need guidance.</b>

102
00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:21.416
<b>I am just a remembrance away.</b>

103
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.083
<b>A festival arrives,</b>

104
00:07:28.083 --> 00:07:31.875
<b>and the whole family remembers me together.</b>

105
00:07:31.875 --> 00:07:34.041
<b>There's an auspicious occasion at home,</b>

106
00:07:34.041 --> 00:07:37.500
<b>everyone joins in my worship.</b>

107
00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:40.250
<b>At the beginning of any good work,</b>

108
00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.958
<b>the family seeks my blessings.</b>

109
00:07:44.958 --> 00:07:48.125
<b>Whenever you remember me,</b>

110
00:07:48.125 --> 00:07:50.750
<b>it brings me joy,</b>

111
00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:56.625
<b>for I have affection for you all.</b>

112
00:07:56.625 --> 00:08:03.291
<b>But will you remember me </b>
<b>only during auspicious times?</b>

113
00:08:03.291 --> 00:08:05.833
<b>Often people think</b>

114
00:08:05.833 --> 00:08:14.583
<b>they can connect with me only through lengthy</b>
<b>spiritual practices during peaceful moments,</b>

115
00:08:14.583 --> 00:08:25.416
<b>or by setting aside extended time with </b>
<b>family for devotional songs and readings.</b>

116
00:08:25.416 --> 00:08:27.916
<b>While these times are appropriate,</b>

117
00:08:27.916 --> 00:08:29.375
<b>but</b>

118
00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:32.625
<b>I've never set such conditions</b>

119
00:08:32.625 --> 00:08:40.041
<b>that only elaborate remembrance</b>
<b>can bring me into your life,</b>

120
00:08:40.041 --> 00:08:42.750
<b>Have I ?</b>

121
00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.250
<b>I have love for you,</b>

122
00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:53.250
<b>so naturally, I wish to help you in moments </b>
<b>of confusion and difficulty too.</b>

123
00:08:53.250 --> 00:09:00.125
<b>But humans, in their troubled times, </b>
<b>wrestling with problems,</b>

124
00:09:00.125 --> 00:09:08.916
<b>sometimes forget that help is</b>
<b>just one remembrance away.</b>

125
00:09:08.916 --> 00:09:13.458
<b>Just remember me for a moment,</b>

126
00:09:13.458 --> 00:09:16.583
<b>and I will manifest in your mind.</b>

127
00:09:16.583 --> 00:09:17.833
<b>And yes,</b>

128
00:09:17.833 --> 00:09:20.625
<b>remember me not just for yourself,</b>

129
00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:23.500
<b>but for your family members too.</b>

130
00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.666
<b>If your life is going smoothly,</b>

131
00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:33.250
<b>but someone in the family is </b>
<b>going through suffering or trouble,</b>

132
00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:38.458
<b>you can remember me for them as well.</b>

133
00:09:38.458 --> 00:09:47.375
<b>It would give me joy to help them by </b>
<b>entering their minds through your prayers.</b>

134
00:09:47.375 --> 00:09:55.458
<b>And along with this, I want you </b>
<b>to consider another thought.</b>

135
00:09:55.458 --> 00:09:58.958
<b>If you are elder in the family,</b>

136
00:09:58.958 --> 00:10:03.958
<b>isn't it possible that your children </b>
<b>or younger family members</b>

137
00:10:03.958 --> 00:10:09.250
<b>remember you only during good times?</b>

138
00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:14.625
<b>Could it be that in difficult situations, </b>
<b>they hesitate to approach you,</b>

139
00:10:14.625 --> 00:10:23.250
<b>fearing they'll receive criticism or </b>
<b>rebuke rather than help?</b>

140
00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.458
<b>Think about it –</b>

141
00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:29.625
<b>anyone can stand with you in good times,</b>

142
00:10:29.625 --> 00:10:30.708
<b>but</b>

143
00:10:30.708 --> 00:10:37.750
<b>family elders' love is needed </b>
<b>most when times are tough.</b>

144
00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:43.750
<b>If they fear approaching you </b>
<b>during bad times, is that right?</b>

145
00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.875
<b>Through your nature and words,</b>

146
00:10:46.875 --> 00:10:55.541
<b>assure them that you stand with</b>
<b>them even in bad times, ready to help.</b>

147
00:10:55.541 --> 00:11:01.208
<b>After the problem is resolved, certainly </b>
<b>give guidance and teach them,</b>

148
00:11:01.208 --> 00:11:02.500
<b>but</b>

149
00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:04.583
<b>in difficult moments,</b>

150
00:11:04.583 --> 00:11:08.708
<b>they need your love and support first,</b>

151
00:11:08.708 --> 00:11:10.500
<b>not reproach.</b>

152
00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.750
<b>You are the family elder,</b>

153
00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.166
<b>you are wise.</b>

154
00:11:14.166 --> 00:11:16.791
<b>Do reflect on this.</b>

155
00:11:21.333 --> 00:11:25.625
<b>I am always present for mankind,</b>

156
00:11:25.625 --> 00:11:26.750
<b>but</b>

157
00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.625
<b>my need becomes greater</b>

158
00:11:30.625 --> 00:11:35.291
<b>when the darkness of unrighteousness </b>
<b>begins to envelope this world.</b>

159
00:11:35.291 --> 00:11:41.458
<b>When humanity becomes</b>
<b>incapable of helping itself.</b>

160
00:11:41.458 --> 00:11:43.083
<b>At such times,</b>

161
00:11:43.083 --> 00:11:45.541
<b>I take avatar.</b>

162
00:11:45.541 --> 00:11:55.833
<b>I stand shoulder to shoulder among humanity, </b>
<b>just as I stand with Arjuna today.</b>

163
00:11:55.833 --> 00:12:00.708
<b>Your workplace is no different.</b>

164
00:12:00.708 --> 00:12:05.208
<b>If you are in a leadership position,</b>

165
00:12:05.208 --> 00:12:14.541
<b>your need becomes greatest when </b>
<b>deep dilemmas arise in your organization,</b>

166
00:12:14.541 --> 00:12:19.083
<b>when your colleagues' morale begins to fall,</b>

167
00:12:19.083 --> 00:12:23.083
<b>when within the organization itself, </b>
<b>like the Kurukshetra,</b>

168
00:12:23.083 --> 00:12:29.333
<b>conflicts between ethics and unethics begin.</b>

169
00:12:29.333 --> 00:12:31.875
<b>There will be many moments</b>

170
00:12:31.875 --> 00:12:37.583
<b>when people will need not only </b>
<b>your verbal guidance,</b>

171
00:12:37.583 --> 00:12:43.708
<b>but when you may need to step </b>
<b>into your former avatar too.</b>

172
00:12:43.708 --> 00:12:50.958
<b>You too were once working at the same level </b>
<b>as those who now work under you.</b>

173
00:12:50.958 --> 00:12:56.541
<b>You know how to solve problems. </b>

174
00:12:56.541 --> 00:12:58.375
<b>Provide guidance,</b>

175
00:12:58.375 --> 00:13:05.791
<b>but if you still feel that your</b>
<b> colleagues' morale is breaking, </b>

176
00:13:05.791 --> 00:13:13.750
<b>sometimes join them shoulder to shoulder, </b>
<b>take the situation in your hands.</b>

177
00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:16.500
<b>Don't just be a senior officer,</b>

178
00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:17.291
<b>but</b>

179
00:13:17.291 --> 00:13:22.250
<b>help them as a fellow worker.</b>

180
00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:24.333
<b>Help them out of their problem.</b>

181
00:13:24.333 --> 00:13:30.000
<b>When people see you standing with them, </b>
<b>they will gain strength.</b>

182
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.333
<b>When they see you solving complications,</b>

183
00:13:33.333 --> 00:13:35.875
<b>they too will awaken to their capabilities.</b>

184
00:13:35.875 --> 00:13:38.541
<b>They will learn from your experience.</b>

185
00:13:38.541 --> 00:13:39.875
<b>And in the future,</b>

186
00:13:39.875 --> 00:13:45.291
<b>this very ability, this capability </b>
<b>will make them self-reliant.</b>

187
00:13:45.291 --> 00:13:51.833
<b>Leadership doesn't just mean sitting </b>
<b>at a higher level giving orders or directions.</b>

188
00:13:51.833 --> 00:13:55.500
<b>Sometimes, stepping down from your position</b>

189
00:13:55.500 --> 00:14:01.333
<b>and working hard in the field</b>
<b>is also part of leadership.</b>

190
00:14:01.333 --> 00:14:03.750
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

